<title>FRANCE: Albright arrives in France ahead of NATO signing.</title>
<headline>Albright arrives in France ahead of NATO signing.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Secretary of State Madeleine Albright arrived in Paris early on Monday ahead of the signing of a security agreement between NATO and Russia aimed at setting terms for their future relationship.</p>
<p>She was due to have lunch with French Foreign Minister Herve de Charette and then a private dinner with Russian Foreign Minister Yevgeny Primakov.</p>
<p>The NATO-Russia agreement is intended to ease the way for eastward expansion of the Atlantic alliance.</p>
</text>
